From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "Gino D." <25200363+zinosaure@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 9 Nov 2026 08:30:41 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] gameflex 0071: the command thread says where its time goes

Every moment of the GPU command thread now belongs to one cause, so the causes add up to its wall
time: its work (PM4, registers, draw glue, programs, resource tables, textures, buffers, targets,
bindings, barriers, Vulkan recording, compilation, transfers, submission, frame upkeep, work handed by
other threads) and its waits (for GPU writes the CPU reads, for resource tables, for remaps, for
presentation, for the completion thread, for the queue lock, for a guest label a pending GPU write will
set, for a label nothing on the GPU will set, idle, idle while the game sits at its suspend point).
Entering a cause suspends the current one (Common::CommandThreadProfile, rdtsc, one writer, no locked
add). Per frame it also counts PM4 packets by opcode, draws, dispatches, barriers, command buffers and
why each was submitted, GPU waits, label waits by kind, polls, blocked retries and Vulkan device memory
allocations, and times each command buffer on the GPU (timestamps at its begin and end: busy time,
idle time with the GPU dry, idle time with work queued). Shown in the performance overlay details,
and every N seconds in the log with --perf-log <seconds>; counted only while either asks. The compact
panel's "CPU waiting on GPU" (every thread, the completion and present threads waiting by design) is
replaced by the command thread's own waits. Host query reset is enabled whenever the device has it.

Astro Bot, Sky Garden, production settings, 8.6 images/s, 116 ms per frame: waits for labels a pending
GPU write will set 35.5 ms (303 per frame), for labels nothing on the GPU sets 11.8 ms (307), textures
13.7, resource tables 12.0, submission 12.1 (55 command buffers, ~0.22 ms each), targets 6.3, draw glue
5.1, buffers 4.5, programs 4.0, recording 2.8, bindings 2.6; the GPU is busy 84 ms and idle 31 ms
waiting for the CPU; 5,250 draws, 26,500 packets, 950 barriers. Wukong 29.2, Tekken 8 30, Clair Obscur
14.8 (no device loss); the instrument costs about 2% while it counts.
